  "report_period": "Week 7 (7th Feb to 14th Feb 2025)",
  "commentary": {
    "bulkers": "Zodiac Maritime have committed their Capesize \"Cape Heron\" 177/2005 Mitsui, Japan (SS/DD 02/2025) & \"Cape Hawk\" 176/2006 Namura & Sasebo, Japan (SS 10/2026, DD 03/2025) to Chinese interests at USD 30 mill enbloc. Note that a week ago, the \"Cape Friendship\" 185/2005 Kawasaki, Japan (SS 03/2027, DD 06/2025) was sold at USD 16,1 mill. Diana Shipping announced the sale of their Post Panamax \"Alcmene\" 93/2010 Jiangsu, China (SS 01/2030, DD 12/2027, Scrubber fitted) to undisclosed interests at USD 11,9 mill. For comparison, the sister vessel \"Pisces First\" 93/2010 Jiangsu, China (SS/DD 12/2025) was sold back in November at high USD 12 mill. Following the acquisition of the Ultramax \"Beechgate\" 63/2019 Iwagi, Japan (SS 03/2029, DD 04/2027) at USD 35,6 mill, clients of Meghna Group have now purchased the one-year-younger sister vessel \"Nord Magellan\" 63/2020 Iwagi, Japan (SS/DD 04/2025) from Tokei Kaiun at a price of low- mid USD 29 mill. Moreover, the \"Sagar Kanta\" 60/2013 Oshima, Japan (SS 03/2028, DD 06/2026) was committed to Indonesian interests at USD 19 mill. Remind you that a month ago, the \"Omishima Island\" 61/2013 Iwagi, Japan (SS/DD 09/2025) was sold at mid-high USD 19 mill. On the Supramax sector, the \"Sagar Shakti\" 58/2012 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS 04/2027, DD 09/2025) was committed to undisclosed interests at high USD 14 mill. For reference, the sister vessel \"Louisianna Mama\" 58/2012 Tsuneishi Zhoushan, China (SS/DD 07/2025) was sold back in September at USD 19 mill. Polsteam have committed their Handysize \"Mazury\" 38/2005 Tianjin, China (SS/DD 04/2025, Ice Class 1C) to Far Eastern buyers at region USD 6 mill, while the sister vessel \"Kujawy\" 38/2005 Tianjin, China (SS/DD 01/2025, Ice Class 1C) was sold back in October at region USD 8 mill. Furthermore, IMECS committed their \"Nord Nanami\" 38/2012 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 06/2025) at USD 13,5 mill. Remind you that the one-year-older sister vessel \"Blue Dragon\" 38/2011 Imabari, Japan (SS/DD 01/2025) was sold back in October at low USD 15 mill.",
    "tankers": "OceanGold Tankers committed their LR2 \"Ocean Phoenix\" 108/2007 SWS, China (SS 10/2027, DD 11/2025) at USD 29,2 mill. In addition, the one-year- older \"Donegal Spirit\" 105/2006 Hyundai, Korea (SS/DD 11/2026) was delivered to clients of IMS at a price of USD 26 mill. The MR1 \"Sunny Star\" 37/2010 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS/DD 05/2025) was committed to clients of Chemnav at low-mid USD 17 mill, while the one- year-older \"Easterly Canyon\" 36/2009 Hyundai Mipo, Korea (SS 07/2029, DD 06/2027) was committed at region USD 16 mill.",
    "freight": {
      "Capesize": "at the level of low-mid usd 6,00's fio range. No period activity to report here.",
      "Kamsarmax / Panamax": "North Pacific rounds ranged at the usd 8,000/10,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 4,000/6,000 pd. A number of Australian trips into China were fixed around usd 10,000/12,000 pd. Indonesian and Australian trips into India were reported at the level of usd 6,000/9,000 pd. South East Asian trips via East Coast South America into China were reported at the level of usd 9,000/11,000 pd. South African trips into India were fixed around usd 10,000/12,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 180K/200K. Continental trips were reported at the level of usd 7,000/9,000 pd. Continental trips via US East Coast into China were fixed around usd 12,000/14,000 pd. Trips from US East Coast into India were reported at the level of usd 13,000/14,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 300K/400K. South American trips into Continent were fixed around usd 13,000/15,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 12,000/14,000 pd plus ballast bonus at the usd 300K/400K. On the period front, a Kamsarmax was reported fixed in the usd 13,850 pd for 4/6 months employment basis delivery China. Also, a Kamsarmax was fixed on a period at the usd 14,000 pd basis delivery China for 12/14 months employment.",
      "Ultramax / Supramax": "Trips from China into West Africa were fixed around usd 6,000/8,000 pd. A number of Indonesian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 7,000/9,000 pd. Indonesian trips into India were fixed around usd 9,000/11,000 pd. Indian trips into China were reported at the level of usd 5,000/7,000 pd. Indian coastal trips were fixed around usd 6,000/7,000 pd. Arabian Gulf trips into US Gulf were reported at the level of usd 5,000/6,000 pd. US Gulf trips into Mediterranean were fixed around usd 14,000/16,000 pd. No period activity to report here.",
      "Handymax / Handysize": "Trips from China into India were fixed around usd 10,000/12,000 pd. Continental trips into West Africa were reported at the level of usd 10,000/11,000 pd Trips from Black Sea into Continent-Mediterranean range were fixed around usd 5,000/6,000 pd. South American trips into Continent were reported at the level of usd 10,000/13,000 pd. South American Coastal trips were fixed around usd 11,000/13,000 pd. South American trips into China were reported at the level of usd 14,000/16,000 pd. No period activity to report here."
    }
  },
